Phase 2 display bring-up, final working state (2026-09-19,
docs/kernel-boot-debugging.md Rounds 38-56): a "samsung,gts7l-ppa957db1-
nt36523" entry in mainline's existing drivers/gpu/drm/panel/
panel-novatek-nt36523.c (not a new driver from scratch - this file
already supports the same NT36523 chip family on Xiaomi's elish, a
directly comparable SM8250 tablet), with a mode timing that's been
proven bit-for-bit correct against a real hardware register readback
pulled live off stock Android's own downstream driver while it was
genuinely streaming real video (Round 56) - the horizontal porches are
deliberately doubled (168/4/60, not the panel's real per-link 84/2/30)
because dsi_timing_setup()'s bonded-DSI code (drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/
dsi_host.c, unmodified/stock) halves them back down for each physical
DSI controller, and this was the actual root cause of the
VIDEO_MDP_FIFO_OVERFLOW that blocked this project for sixteen rounds.

Also: a small drivers/misc/isl98608-gts7l.c for this device's separate
LCD bias IC (two fixed register writes at probe, matching the
downstream driver's own behavior exactly); a board-specific PHY analog
trim override added to drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dsi/phy/dsi_phy_7nm.c
(mirroring dsi_phy_10nm.c's own existing parse_dt_properties/
tuning_cfg precedent) covering all three of downstream's declared
rescode-offset registers (top/bot/mid - "mid" is C-PHY-specific, never
written by mainline's generic path at all) plus vreg_ctrl_0/
str_swi_cal_sel_ctrl, since mainline's generic hardcoded trim constants
for this SoC generation's C-PHY path don't match Samsung's own
downstream calibration for this exact panel/PHY pairing; and
MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST on gts7l_desc's mode_flags, matching
downstream's own qcom,mdss-dsi-traffic-mode = "burst_mode" for this
exact panel. has_dcs_backlight is back to true (Round 46 disabled it on
a since-retracted theory - Round 54 restored it, with the initial
brightness baked into the panel's own prepare()-time init sequence
rather than the automatic post-enable callback, since some DSI
controllers can't reliably take commands once video streaming has
started - a real, documented mainline hardware class, not a novel
theory). Native rate is 96Hz, not this panel's 120Hz default -
dispcc-sm8250.c's MDP core clock frequency table tops out at 460MHz in
mainline, and real 120Hz needs ~523MHz; 96Hz is a first-class
downstream-supported DFPS rate for this panel, not an invented
workaround.

Also registers this project's own DTB in arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/
Makefile (the DTS itself lives at kernel/dts/sm8250-samsung-gts7l.dts
in this repo, synced into a working kernel tree before building; this
patch covers everything else that had to change in the wider kernel
source tree).

All temporary diagnostic pr_err()s added during Rounds 43-56 (in
dsi_host.c, dpu_core_perf.c, dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c, dsi_phy_7nm.c,
isl98608-gts7l.c, panel-novatek-nt36523.c, and the arch/arm64/kernel/
head.S early-boot DRAM marker previously saved as its own patch,
0001-round25-early-dram-debug-marker.patch, now deleted) have been
stripped now that the real root cause is found and fixed - dsi_host.c,
dpu_core_perf.c, dpu_encoder_phys_vid.c, and head.S are consequently
back to pristine mainline and no longer need a diff section at all.

Applies on top of Linux 7.2 (work/linux's checked-out commit
8d3ae59288f1e7d58d76558a6ee96d533bc5019f) with 0002 already applied.

